LINEAR INTERPOLATION
Linear interpolation takes two Vector3s as input and creates a new Vector3 that is a
weighted mixture of the two. In the static 9ector./erp() method, the amount
of each original Vector3 that is used is based on the third argument. Assuming that
Yec$ and YecB are Vector3s:
9ector vecRes = 9ector.Lerp(vecA, vecB, 0.5f);
If the third argument is , YecRes will equal to Yec$; if the third argument is 1,
YecRes will equal YecB. And if the third argument is .f, then YecRes will be
exactly between Yec$ and YecB.
You can find much more information about linear interpolation in the Interpolation
section of Appendix B, "Useful Concepts."
