Object-Oriented Image Creation
First, we'll create the OOP version of our project.
1. From the Assets > Scenes folder of your Project pane, open the _Scene_OOP scene. It
should have all the changes that we made in the "Setting the Scene" section.
2. Select Quad in the Hierarchy.
3. Create and add a new Perlin_OOP C# script to Quad:
a. At the bottom of the Quad Inspector, click the Add Component button.
b. Type Perlin_OOP into the search field of the Add Component pop-up.
c. Click New script.
d. Click Create and Add.
You should now see a Perlin_OOP script in the Project pane and see a Perlin_OOP (Script)
component in the Quad Inspector.
4. Save the scene.
5. Double-click the Perlin_OOP script in the Project pane to open it in Visual Studio.
