I mention avoiding a square root (which computer science students are
often told is inefficient), but if the number you want to take the square root
of is in RAM, it could take 10 times longer to pull it from RAM than to actu-
ally perform the square root. Just something to keep in mind when you're
thinking about avoiding operations that are considered slow in computer
science.
